course: dictionary
lesson: 15815
title: Words with un- and the word uncompleted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can change its meaning. The little word un- at the front means not. So unhappy means not happy, and uncompleted means not completed. Complete means whole and finished, so uncompleted means not finished yet.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. «My uncompleted homework is still on the kitchen table.» The homework is on the table and it has not been finished. The word tells you the work was started, or should be done, but it is not done.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «My unfinished homework is still on the kitchen table.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. Unfinished and incomplete are more common words that mean nearly the same thing.
fact: Uncompleted means not finished; still waiting to be done.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so uncompleted is made from un- and completed.
fact: «Sam had three uncompleted worksheets to finish at break.» This means three worksheets were not finished yet.
fact: «The new bridge was uncompleted when the winter storms came.» This means the bridge was started but not finished.
fact: Incomplete and unfinished are more common words that mean nearly the same as uncompleted.
exercise: «Sam still has three uncompleted worksheets.» What does uncompleted mean? | *Not finished yet | Lost under the desk | Very easy to do | Finished and checked by the teacher
exercise: «The bridge is uncompleted, so the workers are still building it.» What does the sentence tell you? | The workers have gone home for good | The bridge fell down | *The bridge is not finished yet | The bridge has been painted red
exercise: Which word is the opposite of uncompleted? | sad | *completed | started | unfinished
test: «The uncompleted tower has only three floors so far.» Which word means nearly the same as uncompleted? | Tall | *Unfinished | Finished | Painted
test: Priya says her uncompleted worksheet is done. Is she right? | Yes, uncompleted means finished | Yes, it is done | *No, uncompleted means not finished | It depends on the colour of the paper
exam: «The uncompleted road was closed, so we took the long way round.» What does the sentence tell us about the road? | It had been finished last year | It was painted blue | It was a very old road | *It was still not finished
